# Line endings: Windows uses CRLF, Linux and macOS use LF.
# "text=auto" lets Git detect the text files and keep them as LF in the repository,
# whatever the OS of the person who edits them. Binary files (png, ico, icns, jar)
# are detected automatically and are never converted.
# Without this file Git prints "LF will be replaced by CRLF" at every git add.

* text=auto